## 5. `PageAwareBy` – Related Class (Not an Annotation)

`PageAwareBy` is a Healenium locator class that provides similar page-awareness without requiring PageFactory annotations.

### Example

```
import com.epam.healenium.PageAwareBy;

By loginButton = PageAwareBy.by(
    "KioskLabourLogin",
    By.id("loginButton")
);

driver.findElement(loginButton).click();
```

### Difference

| `@PageAwareFindBy`            | `PageAwareBy`                      |
| ----------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| Annotation                    | Java class                         |
| Used with PageFactory         | Used with `driver.findElement()`   |
| Declared on WebElement fields | Created programmatically           |
| Useful in POM                 | Useful in dynamic locator handling |

## 6. Healenium configuration vs annotations

Some commonly discussed Healenium features are configuration properties, not annotations.

Example `src/test/resources/healenium.properties`:

```
heal-enabled = true
recovery-tries = 1
score-cap = 0.5

hlm.server.url = http://localhost:7878
hlm.imitator.url = http://localhost:8000
```

| Property           | Function                                             |
| ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| `heal-enabled`     | Enables or disables self-healing globally            |
| `recovery-tries`   | Controls the number of recovery candidates attempted |
| `score-cap`        | Sets the minimum similarity score                    |
| `hlm.server.url`   | Healenium backend address                            |
| `hlm.imitator.url` | Selector imitator service address                    |

These are documented in the official Healenium-Web setup guide.&#x20;

